# versions/ is committed - it holds what a page looked like before a change, so it can be put
# back byte for byte - but it is NOT part of the site folder on the Mac. Listed here so
# publish.sh's rsync excludes it and its --delete leaves it standing; the files already in it
# stay tracked, .gitignore does not untrack. Adding a new one needs `git add -f versions/...`.
# pages.yml drops the folder from its checkout, so none of it is ever served.
versions/
